# The keys an approval's feedback draft takes (APPROVAL-DRAFT-KEYS). fx
# v0.0.16's draft has no undo, redo or yank: C-y and C-_ are no
# focused-editor key and no approval byte (shortcuts.zig:31-41,
# src/ui/input/runtime.zig:61-73, :103-108@481104fd), a kitty Ctrl+Y is the
# same byte replayed (escape_parser.zig:255-259), and Super+Z and
# Super+Shift+Z are composer undo and redo, no draft action
# (escape_parser.zig:232-234; src/ui/input/runtime.zig:75-96;
# input_approval_runtime.zig:128). So after C-w each of them leaves `ab `,
# and the Enter sends `ab `. Tab in the draft changes nothing and asks for a
# frame (approval_decision.zig:142-143; input_approval_runtime.zig:59-61), so
# Tab and Enter in one write leave the question up (:191-218), and the next
# Enter answers. One `key` line is one tmux send-keys, one write. The turns,
# the workspace and the settings are approvals.cap's.
fx: gateway approvals-fx.json
xfx: gateway approvals-xfx.json
work approvals-ws
fx: seed approvals-fx-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
wait 3
type edit the files
key Enter
wait 3
snap edit-ask
key Tab
wait 0.4
type ab cd
wait 0.6
snap edit-typed
key C-w
wait 0.6
snap edit-ctrl-w
key -H 19
wait 0.6
snap edit-ctrl-y
key -H 1f
wait 0.6
snap edit-ctrl-underscore
key -H 1b 5b 31 32 32 3b 39 75
wait 0.6
snap edit-super-z
key -H 1b 5b 31 32 32 3b 31 30 75
wait 0.6
snap edit-super-shift-z
key -H 1b 5b 31 32 31 3b 35 75
wait 0.6
snap edit-kitty-ctrl-y
key Tab Enter
wait 0.6
snap edit-tab-enter
key Enter
wait 2.5
snap write-ask
gwlog
